&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Zuora&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Zuora, we help businesses grow smarter and adapt faster. Our platform powers modern business models — from subscriptions and usage-based pricing to AI-driven and outcome-based offerings — helping companies launch new products, automate complex billing, and unlock predictable, recurring revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve led the Subscription Economy for more than a decade. Now we’re evolving again by building the definitive platform for quote to cash and helping companies monetize their products and services with an adaptable, AI-ready foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zuora is the finance-first monetization platform for the AI era. As companies adopt usage-based, credit-based, and hybrid business models, Zuora helps them turn pricing complexity into revenue by connecting pricing, billing, payments, collections, and revenue in one system built for finance. We help finance and technology leaders modernize how they design, launch, and scale new revenue models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Partner Marketing, you will turn that opportunity into a repeatable go-to-market motion. You will bring together partner strategy, account-based marketing, seller activation, executive experiences, and disciplined investment to create measurable pipeline and make Zuora easier for partner teams to position and sell.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-visibility role for a strategic, commercially minded marketer who can create clarity across a complex partner ecosystem, influence without direct authority, and turn good ideas into operating rhythm and business results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the joint marketing and pipeline strategy with our key partners.&lt;/strong&gt; Build and govern the annual and quarterly plan with field marketing, sales, partner, product marketing, and other GTM stakeholders. Establish shared priorities, target accounts, owners, milestones, and measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create focused account-based demand.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify the highest-potential segments and accounts, then develop plays with our partners around complex monetization, usage-based and hybrid pricing, and finance transformation. Focus investment where the account opportunity and partner readiness are strongest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activate sellers, partners, and systems integrators.&lt;/strong&gt; Make Zuora easy for partner sellers and system integrators to understand, position, and bring into an account through seller kits, briefings, office hours, joint account planning, and practical enablement. Recognize success through qualified opportunities and pipeline progression, not activity volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn strategic moments into commercial outcomes.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead marketing strategy and activation for key partner events in North America and EMEA, sales kickoffs, field roadshows, CFO forums, webinars, and joint research. Every program should have a clear business objective, target-account hypothesis, activation plan, and post-event conversion path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the operating system and prove what works.&lt;/strong&gt; Establish the shared calendar, cadence, decision rights, intake process, reusable partner kits, and reporting needed for field teams to activate quickly. Manage co-funded programs with clear investment and attribution principles. Report on sourced, influenced, and accelerated pipeline so leaders know what to continue, start, and stop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may be a great fit if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 10+ years of experience in partner marketing, field marketing, demand generation, or a related growth function in B2B SaaS or enterprise technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of creating pipeline through strategic technology partnerships, ecosystems, or co-sell motions, with measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience marketing to CFO, controller, finance transformation, revenue accounting, finance systems, or CIO audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience leading joint plans, seller enablement, account-based programs, and executive experiences with measurable follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring strong budget, agency, co-funded program, and performance-reporting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can influence a large, matrixed partner organization without direct authority, including the judgment to narrow scope, redirect investment, or say no when a program will not create meaningful value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly across executives, sellers, marketers, partners, and technical stakeholders, and can explain complex solutions in simple, compelling language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the independence and operating judgment to create clarity in ambiguous, changing situations without waiting for a playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have (optional):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with Workday or Systems Integrators, and/or experience in ERP transformation, order-to-cash, billing, revenue recognition, or monetization platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with partner deal registration, co-sell governance, and partner revenue models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building global programs that adapt across North America and EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
