&lt;h3&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a North America Field Marketer to lead the planning and execution of integrated field marketing programs that support sales priorities, account engagement, pipeline, and customer growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will own a portfolio of programs, including executive events, partner activations, webinars, tradeshows, and customer engagements, from strategy and initial brief through planning, execution, follow-up, and performance reporting. The ideal candidate is a strategic, hands-on marketer who can translate business and account priorities into effective regional programs, influence cross-functional stakeholders, and deliver measurable results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Sr. Field Marketing Manager, this is a remote position with occasional travel for onsite event support and in-person meetings as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead North America field marketing programs: Develop and execute regional plans aligned to business priorities, Sales objectives, target accounts, partner opportunities, and customer growth goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own program strategy and execution: Manage a portfolio of executive events, webinars, trade shows, partner activations, and customer programs from initial brief through planning, execution, follow-up, and performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive account and Sales alignment: Partner with Sales and Business Development to identify priority accounts, define audiences, and build engagement plans that support pipeline creation, opportunity acceleration, expansion, and customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate stakeholders: Partner with Sales, executives, cross-functional marketing teams, and external agencies to support strategic partners, coordinate joint programs, and deliver high-quality regional activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead program operations and investment: Manage vendors, venues, registration, attendee tracking, lead capture, timelines, purchase orders, and budgets within established guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use marketing and Sales technology: Leverage Salesforce, Marketo, Knak, Outreach, and related tools to improve targeting, program effectiveness, and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure and optimize performance: Track registration, attendance, engagement, meetings, pipeline influence, and other program outcomes; share insights and recommendations with stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve field marketing execution: Build repeatable processes, proactively identify opportunities to improve program quality, and raise the consistency of stakeholder communication and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in field marketing, event marketing, demand generation, or a related B2B marketing role, with demonstrated ownership of integrated programs from strategy through follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop and execute regional or segment-based field marketing plans aligned to business priorities, Sales objectives, and account strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and executing complex B2B programs, including executive, customer, partner, sponsored, and other field marketing events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to partner with Sales and Business Development teams to translate account priorities into audience, invitation, and engagement strategies, including experience with ABM and contact targeting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing vendors, external partners, event logistics, budgets, purchase orders, and multiple concurrent programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Salesforce, Outreach, Marketo, and similar CRM, marketing automation, or campaign management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking, project management, communication, and time-management skills, with the ability to influence without authority, exercise sound judgment, and adapt quickly to changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel occasionally for events and team or stakeholder meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
