&lt;li&gt;HR &amp;amp; Payroll Data Management: Track and review HR payroll interface (PI) files for compensation updates, benefit changes, and new hires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: Work closely with HR, Accounting, Legal, Operations, and third-party vendors to ensure payroll accuracy and resolve discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Support &amp;amp; Communication: Address payroll-related inquiries, providing clear and timely resolutions to employee concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis: Prepare payroll-related financial reports for senior management, Accounting, and Finance teams as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Year-End Processing &amp;amp; Tax Compliance: Assist with year-end reporting and collaborate with payroll vendors to complete international tax filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General Ledger &amp;amp; Accounting: Manage payroll-related journal entries and support month-end and year-end closing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education &amp;amp; Certification: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Accounting, or a related field; Certified Payroll Professional (CPP) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payroll Experience: 5+ years of US payroll processing experience, preferably with ADP, including working with third-party payroll providers, are required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance Expertise: Strong understanding of payroll regulations, tax laws, and international payroll compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Skills: Proficiency in Excel, Word, and MS Office, with experience in payroll software systems. Experience with the implementation of payroll software systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Detail-Oriented: Strong numerical and analytical skills with a keen eye for accuracy in payroll processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Problem-Solving: Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to address employee concerns and collaborate effectively with various teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidentiality &amp;amp; Integrity: Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion and professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organizational &amp;amp; Multitasking Abilities: Proven ability to manage multiple payroll cycles, meet deadlines, and prioritize tasks effectively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Player Mentality: Strong work ethic with a proactive, solution-driven approach to challenges. A desire or willingness to expand knowledge to new areas/geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
